Not only that: even if he has FTP access he is usually not allowed to
use it over the atlantic, due to transmission costs.

But there is a way around: Princeton university set up a FTP server
on BITNET.  Send a normal mail message containing the word HELP to
BITFTP at PUCC.BITNET.  I should mention that this service is already
rather overloaded so that it is probably not wise to use it too
extensively.  But it works, you get the answer within one day.

